statement:
Finite-ring scalar extension commutes with the specified proper and open exchange constituents. The coefficient rings are finite commutative rings in Type (u+1). All functors, scalar comparison maps and equations are those of [def-pur-finite-free-projection-exchange-data]. The exact quantified statement is recorded below.

Precisely (Lean notation, with the stated universes and typeclasses):
theorem scalar_exchange_constituents {A B : Type (u + 1)}
    [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Finite A] [Finite B] (φ : A →+* B) :
    ∀ (pro : Bool) {X' X Y' Y : Scheme.{u}}
      {a : X' ⟶ X} {b : X' ⟶ Y'} {f : X ⟶ Y} {g : Y' ⟶ Y}
      (sq : IsPullback a b f g) (M : Sites.D pro A X),
      ProperExchangeEquation pro φ sq M ∧
      (∀ [IsOpenImmersion f] [IsOpenImmersion b],
        OpenExchangeEquation pro φ sq M)

